# Local session memory: machine paths, never public
CLAUDE.md

# NOTE: prompts/website-publish-queue.json was ignored here until 2026-08-15 because it
# carried absolute machine paths. Its source and figures fields are now repo-relative, so
# it is tracked: the publish record is durable, reviewable, and readable from any clone
# instead of being a local file two sessions happened to agree about.

# Internal session files
AEQ_HANDOFF_CURSOR.md
AEQ_SESSION_HANDOFF*.md
PUNCH_LIST*.md
.cursorrules_bak

# Internal status and audit docs, kept locally, not published
docs/_internal/

# Internal session drafts that a bare `git add -A` keeps sweeping into a public
# repo. Two of these carried /Users/... machine paths. Ignored by name so the
# mistake cannot repeat; the files stay on disk.
prompts/AEQ_handoff_prompt.md
prompts/Cowork_Handoff_AEQ_Session_2026-07-28.md
prompts/Website_Publish_Nudge.md
prompts/profile_README_DRAFT_2026-08-14.md
prompts/v3_Blocker1_Blocker2_Corrections.md

# Build handoff for the local model. Not published; see the file header.
prompts/Hermes_ClaimCheck_Build_Handoff.md

# Internal handoff documents. Pattern, not a file list, because the failure
# this prevents is a NEW handoff getting swept in by a bare `git add -A` before
# anyone lists it. That already happened once: five internal drafts were
# unstaged deliberately, then re-added and published. Matches the same pattern
# the tracked-internal claim-check uses. Force with `git add -f` if one is
# genuinely meant to be public.
*[Hh]andoff*.md
*HANDOFF*.md
